-- title:
--   Faithful local Hecke action on the cohomology module
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, i.e. a two-dimensional $k$-vector space together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q) = \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k$ of that space factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible in the sense that its base change to $\overline{k}$ is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p \in S$, let $N \neq 0$ have all its prime divisors in $S$, let $r$ be a natural number, and assume the weight-two forms of level $N$ have an integral structure (the $\mathbb Z$-lattice [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) spans $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ over $\mathbb C$). Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the Hecke operators attached to $S$ — to $k$, and assume that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (lying in the decomposition subgroup and acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$), one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho.\rho\,\sigma) = X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Finally let $hc_0$ witness `BaseOpComm N r S 𝒪`, i.e. that the operators $\mathrm{baseOp}\,g$ on $H^1(N,\top,\mathcal O)$ commute pairwise as $g$ ranges over [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.Gen N r S`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L11), the set of primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \neq r$. Then there is an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\iota$ from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), the localisation of the Hecke algebra at the submonoid `heckeLocalSubmonoid N S 𝒪 θ`, to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}$ of the module `ML` of the Hecke datum `baseHeckeData N r S 𝒪 θ hc₀` (the datum with generators `Gen N r S`, operators $\mathrm{baseOp}$ and residual system $g \mapsto \theta(T_g)$), such that $\iota$ is injective and, for every generator $g$ and every $m$ in that module, $\iota$ applied to the image of $T_g$ under the structure map $\pi$ sends $m$ to $\mathrm{X}_g \cdot m$, the action of the variable $\mathrm{X}_g$ of the free algebra $\mathcal O[\mathrm{X}_g : g]$ on the module.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura style comparison, at a non-Eisenstein residual eigensystem, of the local anemic Hecke algebra of weight-two cusp forms of level $N$ with the Hecke action on the localised first cohomology of $\Gamma_0(N)$: the former acts faithfully on the latter, and $T_\ell$ acts as the polynomial variable $\mathrm{X}_\ell$. It is used in the passage to auxiliary level and in the freeness statement for the cohomology module over the local Hecke algebra at minimal level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeLocal_exists_algHom_moduleEnd_baseML_injective.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeLocal
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModuleBase
import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_Residual

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
